description: Require CreaGrafana telemetry contract compliance whenever code changes need observability
alwaysApply: true
---

# Telemetry Contract

When creating or changing code, explicitly check whether the change introduces or modifies a handler, request/update path, error path, external call, logging, startup/shutdown behavior, or deployment configuration. If so, add or update telemetry in the same change.

- Read and follow https://github.com/CreaRec/CreaGrafana/blob/main/docs/telemetry-contract.md.
- Use `@crearec/otel`; TripPlanner wiring is in `src/telemetry.ts`.
- Send OTLP only to Alloy. Never send directly to Loki, Tempo, or Mimir.
- Keep `service.name=crea-trip-planner`, `service.namespace=bots`, and set the deployment environment.
- Every handled Telegram update must emit `bot_updates_total` and `bot_handler_duration_seconds` together through `recordHandledUpdate`, including `success`, `error`, and `skipped`.
- Record application failures in `bot_errors_total`; use `bot.handle_update` spans and OTEL logs with explicit severity.
- Measure durations in seconds.
- Metric labels must remain low-cardinality: `result`, `handler`, and `error_type`. Never use IDs, URLs, paths, filenames, trace IDs, or free-text errors as metric labels.
- Telemetry failures must not block business logic.
- New Telegram paths must use the global telemetry middleware, set a short handler enum, and mark skipped or caught-error outcomes where appropriate.
- Add or update tests whenever telemetry behavior changes.

Before finishing any code change, verify whether telemetry was needed and either implement it or confirm the existing global instrumentation already covers the path.
